To find $A$ and $B$, we take the following equation and multiply both sides by the common denominator:

$\begin{align}
\displaystyle\dfrac{3x+1}{x(x+1)}&=\dfrac{A}{x}+\dfrac{B}{x+1}
\\\\
\displaystyle {3x+1}&={A(x+1)}+{Bx}
\end{align}$

Substituting $x=0$, we get $\blueD{A=1}$.

Substituting $x=-1$, we get $\maroonD{B=2}$.
